35
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:53,360
Mr. Northup, I have two gentlemen whose acquaintance you should make.

36
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:55,620
Mr. Brown and Hamilton.

37
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:56,240
Sir?

38
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:59,440
Mr. Northup, these two gentlemen were inquiring...

39
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,960
...about distinguished individuals, and I was just this very moment saying...

40
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,880
...Solomon Northup is an expert player on the violin.

41
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:07,560
He was, indeed.

42
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:09,260
Mr. Moon is being overly gracious.

43
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:12,540
Well, take it into consideration his graciousness and your modesty.

44
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:15,260
May we trouble you for a moment of your time to converse, sir?

45
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:16,180
Of course.

46
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:17,900
Good day.

47
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:19,500
A circus?

48
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,220
That is our usual employee.

49
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:22,900
The company currently in the city of Washington.

50
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:23,580
A circus?

51
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:27,260
Too constricting a word to describe the talented and merry band with which we travel.

52
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:28,720
It is a spectacle.

53
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:29,740
Unlike most...

54
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:30,440
...you've ever witnessed.

55
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:34,260
Creatures from the darkest Africa get unseen by civilized men.

56
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:38,900
Acrobats from the Orient who can tort themselves in the most confounding manners.

57
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:44,700
And I myself, in aid of Mr. Brown, an internationally renowned practitioner in the art of prestidigitation.

58
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:49,980
We are on our way thither to rejoin the company, having left for a short time to make a small profit from our own exhibition.

59
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:51,900
For the reason for our inquiry with Mr. Moon.

60
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:55,380
Yes, we had just a devil of a time in procuring music for entertainments.

61
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,960
Men of true talents are seemingly in short supply.

62
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:58,800
Thank you, sir.

63
00:09:58,800 --> 00:09:59,500
If we could...

64
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:07,200
...wage you to accompany us as far as Washington, we could give you one dollar for each day's services, and three dollars for every night played at our performances.

65
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:12,180
In addition, we will provide sufficient pay for your return here to Saratoga, two weeks from today.

66
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:19,500
Welcome to Washington, Solomon.

67
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:23,700
Good day.

68
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,580
Nintendo, you're too much!

69
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:31,740
